{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01470",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 5.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.54,
      "end_seconds": 12.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "perfect, thanks hello there, so what's the the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.13,
      "end_seconds": 18.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "Um, so... sudden low back pain. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.44,
      "end_seconds": 23.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "When was the the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.13,
      "end_seconds": 29.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Since last weekend, that's when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.14,
      "end_seconds": 39.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.27,
      "end_seconds": 60.45,
      "duration_seconds": 15.18,
      "text": "Only walking, and it's not much. It It happens every other day. I've also had a twinge down the thigh, for about three months. There was stiffness, yes, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 62.48,
      "end_seconds": 71.38,
      "duration_seconds": 8.9,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Heart rate 64, blood pressure 121 over 79. Temperature is 36.7 degrees, respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.08,
      "end_seconds": 74.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.52,
      "end_seconds": 79.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "let's move on to the examination"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.82,
      "end_seconds": 82.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.34,
      "end_seconds": 99.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "the muscles beside the spine are tight and tender and you can lift both legs fully"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.86,
      "end_seconds": 106.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.84,
      "end_seconds": 123.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Any fever, leg weakness, bladder problems or numbness in the groin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.12,
      "end_seconds": 127.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "no, none that I've noticed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.31,
      "end_seconds": 133.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.41,
      "end_seconds": 136.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "No, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.16,
      "end_seconds": 141.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.06,
      "end_seconds": 161.54,
      "duration_seconds": 19.48,
      "text": "I've had an underactive thyroid for about a year now. I have acid reflux, for two years. I've had heart disease, yes. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.0,
      "end_seconds": 175.8,
      "duration_seconds": 12.8,
      "text": "Right, so an underactive thyroid and and acid reflux are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.74,
      "end_seconds": 192.08,
      "duration_seconds": 14.34,
      "text": "I had a triple bypass eight years ago. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.88,
      "end_seconds": 195.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.65,
      "end_seconds": 200.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.99,
      "end_seconds": 204.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "what line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.79,
      "end_seconds": 214.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.53,
      "end_seconds": 219.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.99,
      "end_seconds": 224.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.27,
      "end_seconds": 246.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.95,
      "end_seconds": 248.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "It's thyroxine, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.86,
      "end_seconds": 252.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.3,
      "end_seconds": 263.82,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "75 micrograms, I think that's what's on the box. It's omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.63,
      "end_seconds": 267.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.13,
      "end_seconds": 269.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "For two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.12,
      "end_seconds": 270.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "I follow"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.68,
      "end_seconds": 275.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "I take metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 278.08,
      "end_seconds": 283.22,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 100 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.77,
      "end_seconds": 287.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.93,
      "end_seconds": 297.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. I'm on paracetamol, 1 gram, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.87,
      "end_seconds": 301.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Roughly how long on that one?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.71,
      "end_seconds": 305.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "For two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.49,
      "end_seconds": 310.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.66,
      "end_seconds": 316.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Yes, trimethoprim, it gives me itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.96,
      "end_seconds": 344.44,
      "duration_seconds": 18.48,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is mechanical low back pain. We shouldn't forget a nerve irritation. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had sudden low back pain, since last weekend, and no bladder problems or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.56,
      "end_seconds": 346.26,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.95,
      "end_seconds": 358.94,
      "duration_seconds": 11.99,
      "text": "For this, naproxen, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, five days. You take it by mouth. It's for back pain. Keep moving and walk a little each day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.28,
      "end_seconds": 369.62,
      "duration_seconds": 10.34,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.21,
      "end_seconds": 372.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Alright, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.75,
      "end_seconds": 383.6,
      "duration_seconds": 9.85,
      "text": "Let's review you if it is not better in two weeks. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.75,
      "end_seconds": 387.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.08,
      "end_seconds": 390.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}